Package: open-download-manager
Version: __VERSION__
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: ODM Development Team <dev@odm-project.org>
Depends: libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.10), aria2 (>= 1.34.0), curl (>= 7.80.0), yt-dlp (>= 2024.01.01), httrack (>= 3.49.0)
Recommends: proxychains4, tor, ffmpeg, subliminal
Description: Full-featured download manager for Linux
 Open Download Manager (ODM) is a comprehensive download manager
 designed specifically for Linux systems. It provides advanced download
 capabilities including multi-connection downloads, BitTorrent support,
 video downloads, and website mirroring.
 .
 Key features:
  * Multi-connection HTTP/HTTPS/FTP downloads via aria2
  * BitTorrent and magnet link support
  * Video downloads from YouTube and other platforms via yt-dlp
  * Completion-time subtitle downloads via yt-dlp and Subliminal
  * Website mirroring capabilities via HTTrack
  * Proxy rotation, proxychains and Tor support
  * Clipboard monitoring for automatic download detection
  * Download queue management with pause/resume functionality
  * Native GTK4 interface with system tray support
 .
 Ships a bundled Java 25 runtime; only the GTK4 libraries and download
 tools are required from the system.
